               ship a consent banner at the same time (reject as easy as accept,
               per § 25 TTDSG/TDDDG). Describing tracking before it is live is
               itself a compliance issue.

               <h3>Analytics</h3>
               <p>This website uses [PROVIDER] to understand how the site is used.
               [If it sets cookies or processes personal data such as IP addresses:]
               processing takes place only after you give consent via our cookie banner,
               on the legal basis of Art. 6 (1)(a) GDPR. You can withdraw consent at any
               time with effect for the future via [cookie settings link].
               [For GA4: name Google as processor, note transfer to the USA and the
               safeguard relied upon, and link Google's privacy policy and opt-out.]</p>

               <h3>Cookie consent</h3>
               <p>Non-essential cookies are set only after consent through our cookie
               banner. You can change or withdraw your choice at any time at
               [cookie settings link].</p>
               ============================================================ -->

          <h3>Your rights</h3>
          <p>
            Under the GDPR you have the right to access (Art. 15), rectification (Art. 16), erasure
            (Art. 17), restriction of processing (Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20), and to object to
            processing (Art. 21). Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw that consent at
            any time with effect for the future. To exercise any of these rights, contact
            <a href="mailto:hello@kadanco.com">hello@kadanco.com</a>.
          </p>

          <h3>Right to lodge a complaint</h3>
          <p>
            You have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, in particular in the EU
            member state of your residence, place of work or the place of the alleged infringement. The
            authority responsible for us is the Berliner Beauftragte f&uuml;r Datenschutz und
            Informationsfreiheit.
          </p>

          <h3>Storage duration</h3>
          <p>
            We store personal data only for as long as necessary for the stated purpose or as required by
            statutory retention periods, after which it is routinely deleted.
          </p>

          <p style="margin-top:32px"><a href="/">&larr; Back to homepage</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .legal-hero { padding: 140px 0 64px; }
    .legal-hero h1 { color: #fff; margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .legal-hero .updated { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.72); font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0; }
    .legal-body { padding: 64px 0 104px; background: #fff; }
    .legal { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .legal h2 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); margin: 52px 0 10px; padding-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--periwinkle); }
    .legal h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
    .legal h3 { font-size: 1.12rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 28px 0 8px; color: var(--indigo-deep); }
    .legal p, .legal address { margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.7; }
    .legal address { font-style: normal; color: var(--ink); }
    .legal a { color: var(--indigo); text-decoration: underline; }
    .legal a:hover { color: var(--indigo-deep); }
  </style>
</Layout>